module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.transport_close_read_as_completion

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data transport_close_read_as_completion: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "transport_close_read_as_completion" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a transport close is read as protocol completion** (a consumer of a streamed response decides the response is FINISHED because the connection ENDED, rather than because the protocol's own terminator arrived. ",

    "Every partial answer then presents as a complete one, and the consumer reports success while holding a fragment. ",

    "This is state-space conflation on the completion axis specifically -- `the bytes stopped` and `the sender said it was done` are two facts, and a stream has a third state, SEVERED, that a two-state reading cannot express. ",

    "**SPECIMEN, measured 2026-09-01 by a peer session on its own routing layer.** A streaming SSE client accumulated `message_start`, then a long run of `content_block_delta`, and registered completion in `res.on('end')` UNCONDITIONALLY -- never checking that `content_block_stop`, `message_delta` carrying `stop_reason`, and `message_stop` had arrived. ",

    "A stream severed after 364 thinking deltas therefore produced a well-formed response object containing an intro line and a heading, which the transcript recorded with a tidy `stop_reason` and the UI rendered faithfully as the model's answer. ",

    "**EVERY LAYER DOWNSTREAM OF THE READING LAYER BEHAVED CORRECTLY, AND THAT IS WHY THE TRUNCATION PROPAGATED SILENTLY.** The reading layer did NOT behave correctly -- it is the defect, converting a transport termination into a protocol completion and minting a `stop_reason` no sender had emitted. ",

    "What every layer BELOW it then did was faithful: the transcript recorded the object it was handed, and the UI rendered that object exactly. ",

    "The distinction is the whole diagnostic value of the row -- a defect that hands its consumers a WELL-FORMED artifact recruits every correct layer beneath it into carrying the wrong answer, so correctness downstream is not evidence of correctness upstream. ",

    "It is also why the class survived a full evening of investigation that cleared the UI, the parser, the token budget, and the serving stack in turn: each of those really was innocent, and each exoneration made the true location look less likely rather than more. ",

    "**THE DIAGNOSIS WAS INVERTED FOR HOURS BY THE ARTIFACT THE DEFECT ITSELF PRODUCED.** The fabricated `stop_reason: end_turn` was read at face value as `the model chose to stop`, so the investigation was pointed at the model and at long-context serving -- a lead reinforced by a genuinely large KV allocation -- while the defect sat in the layer doing the reading. ",

    "**RECOGNITION RULE: find the completion predicate and ask whether it names a PROTOCOL EVENT or a TRANSPORT EVENT.** `on('end')`, `on('close')`, process exit, EOF, a read returning zero, and `the socket closed` are transport; a terminator frame, a `done` member, a declared length satisfied, and a trailer are protocol. ",

    "A consumer whose completion predicate is transport-shaped cannot distinguish a finished answer from a severed one, no matter what it does downstream. ",

    "**THE SECOND HALF OF THE RULE IS ABOUT RECOVERY, AND IT IS WHY THE CLASS IS NOT MERELY A MISSING CHECK.** Neither the Messages API nor Ollama's compatibility layer carries a resumption protocol -- no sequence numbers, no cursor, no reattachable session -- so a severed stream cannot be resumed and the only recovery is re-issuing the whole request. ",

    "A client that cannot DETECT truncation therefore cannot retry either, and the missing predicate silently removes the entire recovery arm rather than one diagnostic. ",

    "**THE REMEDY IS ORDERED AND THE ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING**: make truncation a typed refusal FIRST, because until it is detectable a retry cannot be triggered and a fix cannot be verified; only then add re-issue. ",

    "Adding retry first produces a client that retries the errors it can already see and silently accepts the ones it cannot. ",

    "**GUNBC'S OWN EQUIVALENT PATH IS STRUCTURALLY IMMUNE, and the contrast is the useful part rather than a boast.** `gunbc.spark.serving_readback_parse` `spark_serving_parse_generate_done` reads completion from the response's OWN `done` member, and `spark_serving_parse_version_json` refuses a body it cannot parse with `SparkServingReadbackRefused` carrying a typed cause instead of collapsing to an absent reading. ",

    "A severed body there produces a refusal, not a short answer -- the protocol terminator is the predicate, which is exactly the repair the specimen needs. ",

    "**BOUNDED AGAINST NEIGHBOURS.** Against `empty_observation_narrow`: there an observation that could not express what changed renders as `nothing is affected`; here a PARTIAL observation renders as a COMPLETE one, so the count is plausible rather than empty and no zero draws attention. ",

    "Against `absorbing_fallback`: that arm WIDENS on ignorance and is merely expensive; this arm reports a fragment as an answer and is silently wrong, which is below the ladder rather than on it. ",

    "Against `unbacked_execution_claim`: there prose asserts a relation no authority backs; here a machine-generated artifact asserts a completion no protocol event backs, and it is more dangerous precisely because a `stop_reason` field reads as evidence.)",

    "**THE SAME MECHANISM ON THE SESSION-LIFECYCLE AXIS, filed here rather than as a new class because only the axis differs** (calm-eagle-759, 2026-09-05). Substitute a work session for the stream: THE SESSION ENDED and THE OBLIGATION WAS DISCHARGED are two facts, and archiving a session was read as the second. RECEIPT: `dashboard-ops archive` on a lane closed its work item, and that item had been filed specifically to OWN a DESIGN section 4b next-rung trigger. The capability was never delivered; the item closed because the session did. A trigger is retired by its trigger and by nothing else, never by the item tracking it being closed. ",

    "WHAT MAKES THIS AXIS WORSE THAN THE TRANSPORT ONE IS THAT NOTHING IS WRONG AT THE MOMENT IT HAPPENS. A severed stream at least leaves a fragment that a terminator check could contradict. The archive is CORRECT about the session and asserts nothing whatever about the obligation, so there is no field to check and no consumer to disagree -- the loss is of TRACKING, not of data. It is therefore silent everywhere the closed item is not cited. In the receipt it surfaced only because the item id had been written into a pull request body about to merge, where the sentence claiming the trigger had an owner had quietly become false. ",

    "The same archive call had a second effect on a third subject: it orphaned a pull request the lane had published five seconds earlier. The practice repair is to archive on THE LANE'S OWN STATEMENT that it has published nothing, never on a poll taken before the archive call -- a lane that is finishing up is precisely a lane about to publish. Recognition rule for the general axis: when a lifecycle event closes a container, enumerate what the container OWNED that the event says nothing about.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
